# metric-autopsy 0.3.0.dev0 — v0.3 verdicts on the probe truths — git 677d1b8, python 3.13.16, numpy 2.5.3
=== p01 useless, constant and offset metrics
  random-number metric (make_clean)
    metric_validity=UNTESTED | design_adequacy=UNIDENTIFIABLE | effect=NOT_ESTIMABLE | replication=NOT_RUN
    VERDICT: UNIDENTIFIABLE — no estimand pre-registered: declare 'composition' (relative expression) or 'content' (total RNA / genes detected) — the correction depends on it
  constant metric
    metric_validity=DEGENERATE | design_adequacy=UNIDENTIFIABLE | effect=NOT_RUN | replication=NOT_RUN
    VERDICT: DEGENERATE METRIC — the metric returned the same value (0) on every resample, null and perturbation — it carries no information about the data
  GATE 0 on mi_3bin + 0.5: PASS (same as mi_3bin: True; identical shifts: True)
  GATE 0 on mi_3bin + 10: PASS (same as mi_3bin: True; identical shifts: True)
=== p02 sorted G2M vs G1 (2.4x RNA in G2M), plates as replicates
  mean G2M score + injected module
    metric_validity=PASS | design_adequacy=CORRECTED[POWER_NOT_ASSESSED] | effect=DETECTED | replication=NOT_RUN
    VERDICT: SUPPORTED (provisional until replicated)
